---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

/*
 * ariada.org/legal/patent-peace — the canonical, permanently-hosted home of the
 * patent non-assertion pledge referenced from every package NOTICE.
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
 *
 * This page is the single authoritative source of the pledge. Each published
 * package NOTICE reproduces or references this text and names this URL as
 * governing in case of any divergence. The page deliberately speaks of "our
 * pending United States patent applications" generically and reproduces no
 * application numbers, so it carries no patent-disclosure geo-fence wrap.
 *
 * patent-audit-skip: non-assertion-pledge-makes-no-marking-claim-no-app-numbers
 * The only patent text here is the generic word "patent" inherent to a
 * non-assertion pledge. The page asserts NO product is "patented" or
 * "patent pending" and lists NO USPTO application numbers, so it carries no
 * false-marking exposure and needs no geo-fence wrapper.
 *
 * Audience: downstream OSS contributors / fork maintainers and
 * EU public-sector procurement legal reviewers.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Patent non-assertion pledge — ariada.org"
  description="The canonical, permanently-hosted patent non-assertion pledge of Agonist Development AB: a binding, irrevocable, one-way-ratchet commitment not to assert our patents against good-faith open-source users of the @ariada-org packages, additive to the EUPL-1.2 Article 2 grant."
>
  <section aria-labelledby="pledge-heading">
    <h1 id="pledge-heading">Patent non-assertion pledge</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page is the canonical, permanently-hosted home of the patent
      non-assertion pledge that the <code>@ariada-org/*</code> package
      NOTICE files reference. Where any package NOTICE and this page differ,
      <strong>this text governs</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The pledge is made by Agonist Development AB and applies to every
      good-faith open-source user of the published packages. It is written in
      plain words on purpose: a contributor, a fork maintainer, or a
      procurement reviewer should be able to read it once and rely on it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="commitment-heading">
    <h2 id="commitment-heading">The commitment</h2>
    <p>
      Agonist Development AB makes the following binding, public, and
      irrevocable commitment with respect to its published open-source
      packages:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        We will not assert any patent &mdash; including any of our pending
        United States patent applications, and any patents that may later
        issue from them &mdash; against any good-faith user of these packages
        who uses them through their documented public API.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ratchet-heading">
    <h2 id="ratchet-heading">A one-way ratchet</h2>
    <p>
      This pledge is a one-way ratchet: it may be broadened, never narrowed,
      and it survives the conversion of any pending application into a granted
      patent. A user who relies on it today does not lose that reliance if a
      provisional application later matures into an issued patent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="additive-heading">
    <h2 id="additive-heading">Additive to the EUPL-1.2 licence</h2>
    <p>
      This pledge is in addition to, and more generous than, the patent
      licence already granted automatically to every licensee under
      <a
        href="https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/eupl/eupl-text-eupl-12"
        rel="external">Article 2 of the EUPL-1.2</a>. The licence grants the
      patent rights necessary to use the work; this pledge additionally covers
      good-faith open-source users against the broader portfolio.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="reciprocal-heading">
    <h2 id="reciprocal-heading">Reciprocity</h2>
    <p>
      The pledge is reciprocal. It terminates, for a given party, only if that
      party initiates patent litigation alleging that one of these packages or
      its documented use infringes a patent. Good-faith users who do not bring
      such litigation are never affected by another party&rsquo;s conduct.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
    <h2 id="scope-heading">Scope and authority</h2>
    <p>
      The pledge covers the published <code>@ariada-org/*</code> packages when
      used through their documented public API. It is reproduced in full in the
      NOTICE of <code>@ariada-org/wcag-rules-extended</code> and referenced from
      the NOTICE of every other published package. This page is the canonical
      reference for all of them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="links-heading">
    <h2 id="links-heading">Related pages</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/patents">Patent map</a> &mdash; the filed USPTO provisionals and the EUPL-1.2 Article 2 patent peace</li>
      <li><a href="/licenses">License matrix</a> &mdash; per-package SPDX identifiers + rationale</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      Maintained by Alexander Brichkin (Agonist Development AB, Sweden,
      org.nr 559452-5726).
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  blockquote {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
  }
  blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
